#* {{quote-journal|en|year=2004|month=October|title=Don’t Go There! Our Desert-island List of Desert Islands where You’d Never Want to be Stranded|editor=w:Sia Michel|magazine=[[w:Spin (magazine)|Spin]]|location=New York, N.Y.|publisher=[[w:Vibe (magazine)|Vibe]]/Spin Ventures|volume=20|issue=10|page=52|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=neDQuF47lxQC&pg=PA52|column=2|issn=0886-3032|oclc=1242299160|passage=''{{w|Muppet Treasure Island}}'' (1996) Avast! There be no treasure on this island, just a bunch of googly-eyed, synthetic '''scurvies''' staging a bastardized retelling of the classic {{w|Robert Louis Stevenson}} adventure.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|date=13 September 2022|author=Carrie Chang|title=The Dieters: Confessions of a Valley Girl in Plaid|url=https://books.google.com/books?id=ryebEAAAQBAJ&pg=PT20|location=[Bloomington, Ind.]|publisher=w:Xlibris|isbn=978-1-6698-4738-0|passage=Her friends kept writing her warning her that the man market was not that fortuitous, and filled {{quote-gloss|with}} wormies, and '''scurvies''', unctuous bedfellows that would make her chin jut out— {{...}}}}
# {{lb|en|uncountable|by extension|veterinary disease|obsolete}} A [[cattle]] disease, perhaps [[affect#Verb|affecting]] the skin.

====Usage notes====
Before the cause of scurvy was discovered, the word was also used to describe other diseases with similar symptoms.<ref name="OED"/>

